<newsitem itemid="71117" id="root" date="1996-09-23" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Rutland Trust H1 pretax profit drops.</title>
<headline>Rutland Trust H1 pretax profit drops.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		1.71		   vs 1.89</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 0.40		   vs 0.33</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    4.90		   vs 6.86</p>
<p> Turnover		   51.55		  vs 61.30</p>
<p>NOTE - The comparable pre-tax profit for the same period a year ago includes an exceptional profit on disposal of discontinued businesses of 1.98 million stg.  </p>
<p> Exceptional		nil		    vs 1.98</p>
<p> Tax paid		   0.54		   vs 1.52</p>
<p> Net taxed		  4.36		   vs 5.35</p>
<p> Attributable	     4.25		   vs 4.70</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 22</p>
<p> Div registration date  October 15</p>
<p> Ex-div date		October 7</p>
<p>NOTE - Rutland Trust Plc, whose operations range from corporate finance and investment to container port operations and professional services, said comparable half year earnings per share had increased by 44 percent to 1.71 pence from 1.19 pence while profit before tax and exceptional items had been maintained at 4.9 million stg following the disposal of its Leasecontracts business in 1995.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
